{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The data variables `N` and `x` are context inputs only; no top-level data variable appears on the left side of a sampling statement.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only sampling statement is the built-in `multi_normal` prior for the top-level parameter `y`, and the transformed data block uses only unprotected context data.
","model_safe_stan":"// Sample from a Gaussian process using Stan's built in exponentiated quadratic
// covariance function.
// Fixed kernel hyperparameters: rho=1, alpha=1, sigma=sqrt(0.1)

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;
}
transformed data {
  matrix[N, N] K = gp_exp_quad_cov(x, 1.0, 1.0);
  vector[N] mu = rep_vector(0, N);
  for (n in 1 : N) {
    K[n, n] = K[n, n] + 0.1;
  }
}
parameters {
  vector[N] y;
}
model {
  y ~ multi_normal(mu, K);
}
